{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557878-beast-within-merit-flaw","id":1557878,"title":"Beast Within merit / flaw?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-24T11:15:35-08:00","id":1557878,"title":"Beast Within merit / flaw?","content":"In W20 at least (though probably other editions), one of the listed effects of Rage is &quot;the Beast Within&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>W20 145</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Occasionally, a Garou is more a snarling monster than man or beast, and she must pay the price for it. For every point of Rage a character has above her Willpower rating, she loses one die on all social-interaction rolls. People, even other werewolves, can sense the killer hiding just under her skin, and they don\u2019t want to be anywhere near it.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Are there any Merits or Flaws which adjust your effective Rage score just for this effect? I wasn't able to find any from the W20 lists I was able to find, but maybe an equivalent in another edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-24T12:56:34-08:00","id":1557881,"title":"","content":"Nope, I'm afraid not. You've just got to pump up your WP if you want to have a functional character with high Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-24T14:43:11-08:00","id":1557883,"title":"","content":"Or add Rage above your WP if you want to more dysfunctional character since flaws were also mentioned.<br /> <br /> I think part of the reason there are no Merits/Flaws around this is because Rage and WP are already very cheap traits to buy at character creation. Why pay 2 freebies for a Merit that increases your effective Willpower by 3 for the Beast Within rules, when you could get two real dots of WP for the same price, or one extra freebie point for the same level of protection of your social rolls. Actual WP dots are going to do way more for you than effective rating for a specific situation; unless the effective rating is a huge leap (and going over 10 has no impact here).<br /> <br /> There just isn't a lot of space for the level of granularity you'd want for some Merits/Flaws to occupy this niche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}